%N A400976 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(-6,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to -6. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400976 Closed under multiplication; see A400096 for details.
%H A400976 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400976/b400976.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2527</a> (all terms <= 10^10)
%e A400976 Powers of 7 are terms: 7^n -> 7^(n-1) -> ... -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400976 59 is a term: 59 -> 29 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400976 197 is a term: 197 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400976 762332681442053 is a term: 762332681442053 -> 49 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400976 90179616936384011 is a term: 90179616936384011 -> 49 -> 7 -> 1.
%t A400976 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400976 Select[Range[50000], okQ[#, -6] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
